---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---

<DocsLayout title="Password Authentication">
  <h1>Password Authentication</h1>
  <p>
    Email + password is the default first-factor flow. Hashing uses bcrypt
    cost 12 (≈250&nbsp;ms on modern hardware). Plaintext passwords are
    never logged and never stored.
  </p>

  <h2>Sign up</h2>
  <p>
    <code>PasswordSignup</code> creates a new user with the supplied email
    and password and returns access + refresh tokens for a fresh account.
    The optional <code>recovery_email</code> is used by the
    <code>RequestPasswordReset</code> flow.
  </p>
  <p>
    Self-serve signup is enumeration-safe. If the email already belongs to
    an account, the RPC still returns a generic success-shaped response and
    sends a notice email to the existing address instead of returning
    <code>already_exists</code>. Treat signup as account-creation intent,
    not as a reliable account-existence probe.
  </p>
  <Code code={`curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.v1.IdentityService/PasswordSignup \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{
    "email": "alice@example.com",
    "password": "correct horse battery staple",
    "recoveryEmail": "alice@personal.example"
  }'`} lang="bash" />

  <h3>Errors</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Condition</th><th>Code</th></tr>
    <tr><td>invalid email</td><td><code>invalid_argument</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>password fails strength check</td><td><code>invalid_argument</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GATEWAY_AUTH_ALLOW_LOCAL=false</code></td><td><code>permission_denied</code></td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Log in</h2>
  <p>
    <code>PasswordLogin</code> verifies credentials and either returns
    tokens directly or, when the user has TOTP enabled, returns
    <code>totp_required: true</code> with a <code>login_challenge_id</code>
    that the client passes to <code>VerifyTotp</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Local password login does <em>not</em> require prior email verification.
    A newly signed-up user may log in immediately and complete email
    verification later.
  </p>
  <Code code={`curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.v1.IdentityService/PasswordLogin \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"email":"alice@example.com","password":"correct horse battery staple"}'`} lang="bash" />
  <p>Response (no 2FA):</p>
  <Code code={`{
  "user":         { "id": "user_...", "email": "alice@example.com", ... },
  "accessToken":  "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "refreshToken": "rt_...",
  "expiresIn":    900
}`} lang="json" />
  <p>Response (TOTP enrolled):</p>
  <Code code={`{
  "user":             { "id": "user_...", "email": "alice@example.com", ... },
  "totpRequired":     true,
  "loginChallengeId": "lc_..."
}`} lang="json" />
  <p>
    See <a href="/identity/docs/auth/totp">TOTP (2FA)</a> for completing
    the challenge.
  </p>

  <h2>Lockout</h2>
  <p>
    After <code>GATEWAY_LOGIN_MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS</code> consecutive
    failures (default 5), <code>PasswordLogin</code> returns
    <code>account temporarily locked</code> for
    <code>GATEWAY_LOGIN_LOCKOUT_SECONDS</code> (default 900) before
    accepting another attempt. Successful login resets the counter.
  </p>

  <h2>Change password</h2>
  <p>
    Authenticated users change their password via
    <code>ChangePassword</code>. The current password is required; on
    success the password hash is updated and (per audit policy) all
    sessions other than the caller's are revoked.
  </p>
  <Code code={`curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.v1.IdentityService/ChangePassword \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"currentPassword":"old","newPassword":"new pass phrase 47"}'`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>Forgot password</h2>
  <p>
    Identity does not expose a self-serve "forgot password" form. Two
    paths:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Recovery-email flow</strong> via
      <code>RequestPasswordReset</code>. If the user has a
      <code>recovery_email</code> set, a one-time reset token is emailed
      to that address. If not, the call still returns success (no
      enumeration). See <a href="/identity/docs/auth/invitations">Invitations</a>
      for how the token gets consumed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Admin help</strong> via <code>RequestAdminHelp</code>. Users
      who can't get in raise a ticket; an admin resolves it through
      <code>ListHelpRequests</code> + <code>ResolveHelpRequest</code> from
      the dashboard.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Disabling password auth</h2>
  <p>
    Set <code>GATEWAY_AUTH_ALLOW_LOCAL=false</code> to make the deployment
    OAuth-only. <code>PasswordSignup</code> and <code>PasswordLogin</code>
    will return <code>permission_denied</code>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
